<p>Pope Leo XIV drew about 120,000 worshippers to an open-air Mass at Japoma Stadium in Douala on Friday, using the biggest event of his Cameroon visit to urge people to reject violence, abuse, and division and instead become builders of peace. He also spoke directly to young Africans, urging them to resist corruption and what he called the temptation to leave home. Instead, he encouraged them to develop their talents and work for change in their own communities. The visit underscored both the Vatican&#x27;s concern over conflict and the strong response from Cameroonian Catholics, who turned out in large numbers for a message centered on peace, perseverance, and civic responsibility.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/WbVYb2ZqTxPDntabWkk5rVc7udScsDpHhqZwY85ZZsIKlN3qtdNxLbGjjhAbCKf6UEZb9tWFtRRbz450EjjmPdb2BsKP22gwa-tSxjxVnznpQXNE9X-ACjXtxTCSeAqpSa46KQJgakN0EimlBmVc-EZZXQn6KOrG9a0LLAZYyA' alt='Pope Leo XIV during his Cameroon visit, where he celebrated a large open-air Mass in Douala.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Biblical imagery: PBS said Leo drew on the story of Jesus multiplying the loaves as he urged young people to develop the gifts they already have.</li><li>Crowd expectations: ABC&#x27;s advance coverage said up to half a million people were expected at the papal Mass, showing just how much anticipation surrounded the visit.</li><li>Tour schedule: BBC reported that Leo was on his third day in Cameroon on Friday and was due to travel to Angola on Saturday as part of his four-nation Africa trip.</li></ul><blockquote>Multiply your talents through the faith, perseverance, and friendship. - Pope Leo XIV</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pope Leo XIV: SCMP said he paired his appeal against violence with a call for Cameroonians to show generosity to their neighbours. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3350542/pope-urges-cameroon-reject-violence-mass-draws-120000-people'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Young Cameroonians: PBS showed that Leo framed staying home as an active challenge — building talent locally and rooting that appeal in faith, perseverance, and friendship rather than frustration alone. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/pope-urges-young-people-to-resist-temptation-of-corruption-in-big-mass-in-cameroon'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Cameroonian faithful: The warmth of the welcome was visible even before the liturgy, with some believers reaching Japoma Stadium the day before and spending the night outside to secure a place. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3350542/pope-urges-cameroon-reject-violence-mass-draws-120000-people'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3350542/pope-urges-cameroon-reject-violence-mass-draws-120000-people'>Pope urges Cameroon to reject violence at mass that draws 120,000 people</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cdj7kwn1d78o'>Thousands celebrate open-air Mass with Pope Leo in Cameroon - in pictures</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/half-million-people-expected-pope-leo-xivs-mass-132127984'>Pope urges Africa&#x27;s youth to resist temptations of migration, corruption in Cameroon</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-to-cameroon-s-faithful-reject-violence/a-76835789'>Pope Leo XIV to Cameroon&#x27;s faithful — &#x27;reject violence&#x27;</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/pope-urges-young-people-to-resist-temptation-of-corruption-in-big-mass-in-cameroon'>Pope urges young people to resist temptation of corruption in big Mass in Cameroon</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>